DESCRIPTION:The Wake Forest Renaissance Centre\, 405 S. Brooks St.\, Wake F
 orest\, NC\, is inviting artists of all ages\, abilities\, and mediums to 
 submit an original work of art that answers the question\, “What does Am
 erica mean to you?” for its America 250 Art Exhibit. The submission dead
 line is Sunday\, May 24.\n\nDesigned to give visual artists an opportunity
  to display and sell their work in a gallery setting\, the exhibit will in
 clude 64 linear feet of hanging space and a medium-sized display cabinet t
 o showcase 2D and 3D works for art.\n\nSelected works of art will be displ
 ayed in the Renaissance Centre Arts Annex Monday\, June 8\, through Friday
 \, July 17.\n\nThe Renaissance Centre will honor the artists and their wor
 ks during a special reception on Friday\, June 12\, from 6-8 p.m. in the R
 enaissance Centre Arts Annex. The reception is free and open to the public
 \, and works will be available for purchase through the artists. For more 
 information\, contact RC Arts Coordinator April Cannon at 919-435-9568.\n\
 nSubmit Your Artwork: https://online.wakeforestnc.gov/Forms/America250Exhi
 bitionSubmission
GEO:35.974177;-78.508713
LOCATION:Wake Forest Renaissance Centre Annex
SUMMARY:America 250 Art Exhibition
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/america-250-art-exhibition
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
END:VEVENT
