DESCRIPTION:In honor of Juneteenth\, genealogist Trisha Blount will share f
 reedom stories of Greene County men who joined the U.S. Colored Troops (US
 CT) and research methods for tracing African American genealogy from ensla
 vement through the Civil War and into Reconstruction. Using records from t
 he State Archives of N.C.\, alongside federal service records\, Freedmen's
  Bureau records\, and National Archives pension files\, participants will 
 learn about individuals and contraband camps\, like the Trent River settle
 ment. Register by June 30.
