DESCRIPTION:Step Into 1776: Downtown Goldsboro to Come Alive with Revolutio
 nary History This July 3\n\nThis Independence Day weekend\, the past will 
 come alive in downtown Goldsboro as the Wayne Community College Foundation
  invites the community to experience “Step Into 1776: A Revolutionary Jo
 urney Through America’s Founding Era”—an immersive living history ev
 ent celebrating America 250 and the spirit of the nation’s founding.\n\n
 Taking place on Friday\, July 3\, this family-friendly event will transfor
 m downtown Goldsboro into an interactive colonial experience filled with r
 eenactors\, live demonstrations\, music\, and hands-on educational exhibit
 s. Designed for all ages\, Step Into 1776 offers a rare opportunity to exp
 erience daily life during the Revolutionary War era and gain a deeper appr
 eciation for the people and sacrifices that shaped America’s independenc
 e.\n\nVisitors can expect to encounter British and Patriot soldiers throug
 hout downtown\, interacting with the public and bringing history to life t
 hrough authentic uniforms\, gear\, and storytelling. Reenactors from acros
 s North Carolina will be on-site portraying soldiers\, civilians\, craftsp
 eople\, and historical figures from the late 18th century.\n\nOne of the d
 ay’s most anticipated attractions will be the live weapons demonstration
 s at Freedom Field\, scheduled for 2:00\, 3:00\, 4:00\, and 5:00 p.m. Gues
 ts will witness demonstrations featuring muskets and a live cannon\, offer
 ing a powerful glimpse into the realities of Revolutionary-era warfare.\n\
 nBeyond the battlefield\, attendees will explore what everyday life looked
  like in 1776. At the Terrace Room\, guests can enjoy demonstrations focus
 ed on colonial crafts\, women’s fashion\, and domestic life. At the CSS 
 Building/ACME Theater\, visitors can observe a fascinating—and sometimes
  startling—look at 18th-century battlefield medicine and surgery\, highl
 ighting how dramatically healthcare has evolved over the last 250 years.\n
 \nLocal downtown merchants are also joining in the celebration by offering
  themed treats\, patriotic specials\, and Revolutionary-era memorabilia at
  their businesses\, creating even more opportunities for visitors to engag
 e with the event as they explore downtown Goldsboro.\n\nGuests can also st
 op by the Colonial Tavern\, located at The Filling Station\, to enjoy beve
 rages and socialize in a colonial-inspired setting. Throughout the afterno
 on\, the sounds of drum and fife music will echo through downtown streets\
 , transporting visitors back to a time of revolution\, resilience\, and th
 e birth of a nation.\n\nThe evening will conclude at the Paramount Theatre
  with a special ticketed experience called “Taste the Revolution\,” wh
 ere guests can enjoy Revolutionary-inspired food and refreshments before a
  screening of the classic musical film 1776. The food experience offers at
 tendees a unique opportunity to literally taste flavors inspired by Americ
 a’s founding era before settling in for an entertaining and thought-prov
 oking look at the signing of the Declaration of Independence.\n\n“This e
 vent is about more than just history—it’s about connection\,” said J
 acqueline Kannan\, Executive Director of the Wayne Community College Found
 ation. “We want people to walk through downtown and truly feel immersed 
 in the sights\, sounds\, and stories of 1776. Whether you’re a history e
 nthusiast or simply looking for a unique family outing\, there will be som
 ething memorable for everyone.”\n\nThe Wayne Community College Foundatio
 n created Step Into 1776 to celebrate America’s 250th anniversary while 
 bringing education\, culture\, and community together in a meaningful way.
 \n\nAdmission to the living history portion of the event is open to the pu
 blic. Community members are encouraged to wear patriotic colors\, bring th
 e family\, and prepare to step back in time for an unforgettable Revolutio
 nary journey.
LOCATION:Downtown Goldsboro\, NC
SUMMARY:Step Into 1776
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/step-into-1776
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Ceremonies & Anniversaries
END:VEVENT
