DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Independence Day and the nation’s Semiquincentennia
 l with Island Farm! Island Farm will host visitors to celebrate the holida
 y. Attendees are encouraged to bring a picnic lunch to enjoy on the Farm
 ’s grassy lawn\, and continue celebrations of the nation’s birth with 
 musket-fire\, traditional games\, a reading of the Declaration of Independ
 ence\, and much more.\n\n \n\nA living history farm\, Island Farm is a tan
 gible glimpse into coastal history\, and the realities of life on Roanoke 
 Island in the mid-1800’s. Admission to the site is $11\, and children 3 
 and under are admitted for free. The site is located at 1140 N US Highway 
 64\, north of Manteo on Roanoke Island.\n\nIsland Farm is owned and operat
 ed by Outer Banks Conservationists\,  non-profit organization founded in 1
 980 to protect important natural\, cultural\, and historic resources along
  North Carolina’s Outer Banks through education and conservation. For mo
 re information\, visit https:obcinc.org/visit-our-sites/island-farm/\, ema
 il info@obcinc.org or call 252-473-6500.
GEO:35.928825;-75.687443
LOCATION:Island Farm
SUMMARY:Independence Day Celebrations at Island Farm
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/independence-day-celebration
 s-at-island-farm-9510
