BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260731T040425Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51585555363180
DTSTART:20260704T140000Z
DTEND:20260704T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Experience the best of North Carolina with DNCR at Capitol 250:
  NC Freedom Fest!  \n\nThis free\, all-day festival is a celebration of th
 e arts\, history\, nature\, and culture that define North Carolina’s rol
 e in the nation’s story.\n\nDon’t miss live musical performances throu
 ghout the day\, sponsored by Bank of America.\n\nHeadlining Musical Perfor
 mances by:\nTIFT MERRITT & RISSI PALMER\n\nAdditional live performances by
 :\nNest of Singing Birds\n82nd Airborne All-American Brass Quintet\nWake &
  District Raleigh Pipe Band\nN.C. Governor’s School Choir\nPoet Zack Zac
 hary\n\nIn addition to live music and cultural performances\, the festival
  features loads of family-friendly fun including:\n\nHurricanes KidZone\, 
 sponsored by the Carolina Hurricanes\nTrolley tours of historic downtown R
 aleigh\nLiving history and special exhibits\nMore than 50 vendors and food
  trucks\nIndependence Day Ceremony\n\nThis downtown Raleigh celebration wi
 ll complement a morning parade organized by the N.C. Department of Labor a
 nd evening fireworks at Dix Park organized by the City of Raleigh.\n\nThis
  event is free and open to the public. We hope to see you there!
GEO:35.780436;-78.639951
LOCATION:State Capitol
SUMMARY:Capitol 250: North Carolina Freedom Fest  
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/july-4th-capitol
