DTSTART:20260707T143000Z
DTEND:20260707T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Come out to Harper Library while we commemorate the 250th anniv
 ersary of the signing of the Declaration of Independence in a 3-part serie
 s.\n\nThomas Jefferson was the principal author of the Declaration of Inde
 pendence\, which created the United States. To celebrate the Declaration's
  upcoming 250th birthday on July 4\, 2026\, Monticello\, the Jefferson hou
 se\, is launching Declaration Book Club\, featuring short readings\, livel
 y videos\, and probing questions to spark discussion of our past\, present
 \, and future as one people\, created equal. This series explores what Jef
 ferson and his cosigners declared in 1776--and how do you pursue life\, li
 berty\, and happiness today.\n\nAt each meeting we will watch videos\, dis
 cuss reading material and discuss a list of predetermined guided questions
  pertaining to each sessions materials.\n\nEach participant who signs up w
 ill receive a separate email for each session that includes the optional r
 eading materials\, suggested supplemental reading materials\, and the guid
 ed questions we will go over for each meeting.\n\nMeeting 1: 1776\nMeeting
  2: 1826\nMeeting 3: Legacies\n\nRegister online @ https://brunsco.libcal.
 com/event/16359612 or call 910-253-1813\n\nSponsored by Friends of the Lib
 rary Southport Oak Island
GEO:33.917773;-78.019919
LOCATION:Margaret & James Harper Jr Library
SUMMARY:Monticello Book Club
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/monticello-book-club
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Panels & Book Discussions
END:VEVENT
