DESCRIPTION:The 250th Exhibit is a themed exhibit that is a showcase featur
 ing visual art\, as inspired by the United States Semiquincentiennial\, wh
 ich is the 250th anniversary of the United States Declaration of Independe
 nce. The theme is up to the artist’s interpretation\, and he/she may sub
 mit any work as long as it fits somehow with the media\, subject matter or
  presentation of the 250th. \n\nSome examples include\, but are not limite
 d to: an art piece inspired by the time period during and/or the actual si
 gning of the Declaration of Independence\, an art piece about a significan
 t historical event in the United States\,or an art piece about how art has
  played a major role in the culture of the United States over the last 250
  years. This exhibit will be on display in the Depot’s Center Gallery.
GEO:35.582781;-80.812786
LOCATION:Mooresville Arts at the Depot
