X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260731T040426Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52922776109452
DTSTART:20260715T060000Z
DTEND:20260715T073000Z
DESCRIPTION:Free Online lecture and live Q&A from Road Scholar\n\nWe now th
 ink of George Washington as America’s foremost patriot\, but he came to 
 accept war and independence only slowly. Far from embracing his selection 
 as commander-in-chief\, he feared it would lead to his ruin — and possib
 le death. Join author and historian Dr. Edward Lengel as he explores how W
 ashington’s hope for America’s future led him to take on leadership in
  the struggle for independence. Celebrate the United States of America’s
  250th anniversary in 2026 through the lens of Washington’s leadership i
 n the Revolutionary War.
GEO:33.922523;-78.578901
LOCATION:Southwest Brunswick Branch Library\, Center Pit
SUMMARY:George Washington: The Road to Independence
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/george-washington-the-road-t
 o-independence
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
