DTEND:20260718T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s 250th Anniversary at the Lewisville Branc
 h Library with a day of history brought to life!\n\nStarting at 11 a.m.\, 
 Professor Bill Partin will present Revolutionary Women: Heroines of the Am
 erican Revolution and discuss the courage\, intelligence\, and influence o
 f women who helped shape our nation’s fight for independence. \n\nAt 1 p
 .m.\, step into the past with our live and interactive wax museum\, where 
 visitors can “meet” and converse with figures from the Revolutionary e
 ra. \n\nAlso\, at 1 p.m.\, children can drop in to create patriotic arts a
 nd crafts at our monthly Mini Masters Art Adventures program located in ou
 r Storytime Room. \n\nConcluding at 3 p.m.\, The Battle of Shallow Ford: A
 n Exhibition of Words and Watercolors. This blends storytelling and waterc
 olor to interpret a pivotal local Revolutionary War event.  \n\nRick Jones
 ’s watercolors and Marilyn Ingram’s researched storyboards tell the st
 ory of the Revolutionary skirmish at the Shallow Ford. The work draws on s
 ources including the North Carolina State Archives and features scenes of 
 the ford\, nearby Moravian settlements along the Great Wagon Road\, and th
 e Huntsville commemoration.  \n\nRefreshments will be served during the ex
 hibition.
GEO:36.096535;-80.420124
LOCATION:Lewisville Branch Library \, Auditorium and Storytime Room
SUMMARY:Echoes of 1776
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/echoes-of-1776
