DESCRIPTION:Join us as we celebrate the impactful partnership between NC St
 ate Parks\, Friends of State Parks\, and Waypoint Adventure — bringing i
 nclusive outdoor recreation programs to visitors with disabilities since 2
 024! \n\nIn honor of Disability Pride Month and National Disability Indepe
 ndence Day (July 26)\, enjoy a day at Lake James State Park\, where you'll
  hear about the impact of this partnership from representatives of NC Stat
 e Parks and Waypoint Adventure.\n\nCome enjoy a cookout lunch\, learn more
  about this program\, and participate in hands-on demos of the adaptive hi
 king and kayaking equipment that help make our parks more accessible for a
 ll.\n\nEvent Contact: Kris Anne Bonifacio\, krisanne.bonifacio@ncparks.gov
 \n\nAbout Waypoint Adventure\n\nWhere “I can’t” becomes “Yes\, I c
 an”\, Waypoint Adventure is a non-profit educational organization that a
 wakens youths and adults with disabilities to their willful spirit through
  the power of adventure. With guided\, experiential programs tailored to m
 eet people right where they’re at\, Waypoint Adventure provides personal
  growth and team triumph – as participants discover their purpose\, valu
 e\, strengths\, and abilities. Waypoint Adventure is here to help free wha
 t’s possible. \n\nVisit our website to learn more and get involved with 
 Waypoint Adventure today!
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park\, Swim Beach at Paddy's Creek Access
SUMMARY:Celebration of Access at North Carolina State Parks
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/celebration-of-access-at-nc-
