DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered which native plants attract which pollin
 ators\, or are you hoping to welcome specific pollinators to your garden? 
 Join staff from the Library of North Carolina’s Government and Heritage 
 Library and the NC Museum of Natural Sciences for a Native Plant Walk focu
 sing on the connections between native plants\, pollinators\, and plant mo
 rphology.\n\nThis plant walk will explore the NC Department of Natural and
  Cultural Resources’ Native Plant Meadow and the NC Museum of Natural Sc
 ience’s Native Plant Garden. The event will take place primarily outdoor
 s\, with participants traveling approximately ½ mile round-trip via paved
  sidewalks. \n\nRegistration is requested. \n\nThis event is hosted in con
 nection with the GHL's Native Plant Seed Library. Learn more about our see
 d library at slnc.info/seeds\, and more about seed libraries and native pl
 ants on our GHL Seed Library Research Guide at slnc.info/seedlibraryguide.
  \n\nOur Native Plant Walks and related events count toward the Office of 
 Environmental Education's Environmental Educator Certification. This event
  qualifies for two hours of Criteria II credit. \n\nQuestions about this e
 vent? Contact us at ghl.info@dncr.nc.gov.
GEO:32.071865;-81.092949
LOCATION:NC Government and Heritage Library and DNCR Jones Street Gardens
SUMMARY:July Native Plant Walk: Pollinators and Plant Morphology 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/july-native-plant-walk-polli
 nators-and-plant-morphology
