DTSTAMP:20260731T040427Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52630107404110
DTSTART:20260727T140000Z
DTEND:20260727T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, July 27th\, 2026 | 10am - 3pm\nMountain Gateway Museum
 \n78-C Catawba Avenue\, Old Fort\, NC\, 28762\n\nApply here! Applications 
 close on Tuesday\, May 26th\, 2026.\n\n\n***Attending middle grades teache
 rs will receive $100 stipend + Lunch + .5 CEUs -- Open to middle grades te
 achers in McDowell\, Burke\, Mitchell\, Yancey\, Rutherford\, and Madison 
 Counties. \nJoin the North Carolina Department of Natural and Cultural Res
 ources (DNCR) for an exclusive afternoon for area middle-grades educators 
 at Mountain Gateway Museum!\n\nThe Mountain Gateway Museum explores and ce
 lebrates the cultural history of Western North Carolina\, an area spanning
  38 counties from the Blue Ridge Mountains to the Piedmont. When visiting 
 the museum or utilizing it's resources\, students will experience the Sout
 hern Appalachian past and learn about the people and culture that shaped t
 he western region of North Carolina. \n\nAttending educators  will preview
  the various on-sight activities that can be offered and tailored for visi
 ting school groups\, as well as classroom outreach opportunities. Time wil
 l also be provided for attending teaches to share feedback\, ideas and req
 uests regarding what else you would like our site to offer in support of c
 lassroom learning. Attendees will also receive information about DNCR reso
 urces for educators.\n\nAttending educators will also receive:\n\nA $100 s
 tipend (upon completion of a post-event survey)Lunch.5 CEUsThe chance to n
 etwork with other educators from multiple schools across the district\, as
  well as the opportunity to engage with DNCR/Mountain Gateway Museum staff
  ready to serve as a source of support for your important work in the clas
 sroom!Priority registration will be given to middle school teachers in McD
 owell\, Burke\, Mitchell\, Yancey\, Rutherford\, Madison\, & surrounding c
 ounties but any K-12 teacher is eligible to apply. (Make sure your distanc
 e from the Museum allows you to comfortably arrive by 10 am). Don’t miss
  the opportunity to experience what the Mountain Gateway Museum has to off
 er\, while also enjoying food and fellowship with amazing teaching colleag
 ues from across the region! \nPlease note that late arrivals and early dep
 artures cannot be accommodated. Before submitting an application\, please 
 check your schedule to ensure you can arrive by 10:00am and that you are a
 ble to stay until 3:00pm\n\nSpace is limited to 20 registrants\; filling o
 ut this form does not guarantee your registration. Participants will be re
 gistered based on a combination of ensuring a diversity of schools and gra
 de levels represented\; the order in which your application was received p
 er school\; and your application responses and completeness. You should re
 ceive a response to your application no later than May 29th. If after May 
 29th you have not received a response and a message is not in your junk/sp
 am folder\, please contact us at educationoutreach@dncr.nc.gov.\n\nCANCELL
 ATION POLICY\nDNCR is committed to providing free professional development
  to teachers\, with not even a small fee or deposit required. However\, th
 ese programs are costly to the organizers/funders. Thus\, if you receive a
  space in this event and you find that you need to cancel at any point\, i
 t is critical to let us know immediately and no later than five days befor
 e the event by e-mailing educationoutreach@dncr.nc.gov. Last minute cancel
 lations and "no-shows" with no communication result in waste of budget\, f
 ood\, materials\, etc.\, and prevents wait listed teachers from participat
 ing. Except in the case of an emergency\, if a registered teacher does not
  show up or communicate no longer being able to attend\, your school may b
 e billed for a $75 no-show fee.\n\nQuestions?\n\nContact us at educationou
 treach@dncr.nc.gov\n\n \n\nThis event is funded and hosted by North Caroli
 na Department of Natural and Cultural Resources (DNCR) and Friends of the 
 Mountain Gateway Museum.
GEO:35.627587;-82.180647
LOCATION:Mountain Gateway Museum and Heritage Center
SUMMARY:Educator Workshop: Hands-On History at the Mountain Gateway Museum 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mgmteacherworkshop
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
