UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52920797556498
DTSTART:20260727T140000Z
DTEND:20260727T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:Its that time of year again! Come celebrate the summer at Merch
 ants Millpond State Park with our 4th year of the Summer Junior Adventure 
 Series! In this series\, we have a different topic that we teach about eve
 ry Monday at 10 AM throughout the summer. \n\nThis week special guests fro
 m the Musuem of the Albemarle will be joining us to learn about an often o
 verlooked group\; the Algonquian Native Americans. Participants will disco
 ver the story of the first people to inhabit the Albemarle region: Algonqu
 ian-speaking Native Americans. Learn about the Algonquians’ way of life\
 , including foodways\, shelter\, and clothing\, along with the Algonquian 
 farming heritage as they cultivated the Three Sisters. \n\nThis program wi
 ll begin promptly at 10 AM at the visitor center. All ages are welcome. Gu
 ests are encouraged to dress for the weather as part of this program may b
 e outside.
GEO:36.437278;-76.701271
LOCATION:Merchants Millpond State Park\, Visitor Center
SUMMARY:Museum of the Albemarle - Algonquians: The First Communities of Nor
 theastern North Carolina
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/museum-of-the-albemarle-algo
 nquians-the-first-communities-of-northeastern-north-carolina
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
