DTSTART:20260801T140000Z
DTEND:20260801T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that North Carolina’s first public reading of th
 e Declaration of Independence took place in Halifax on August 1st\, 1776? 
  Join historical interpreters as they reenact events surrounding the joyou
 s news of American independence from Britain. At 12:00pm\, see a reenactor
  portray Cornelius Harnett\, President of the Council of Safety\, read the
  Declaration for the first time in North Carolina. View a screening of The
  American Constitution\, a new documentary film on the writing of the Unit
 ed States Constitution\, which was partially filmed at Historic Halifax. F
 ree.
GEO:36.33002;-77.58941
LOCATION:Historic Halifax
SUMMARY:Independence Comes to NC
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/independence-comes-to-nc
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Ceremonies & Anniversaries
END:VEVENT
