DTSTAMP:20260731T040428Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52702202787039
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DESCRIPTION:May 2–August 9\, 2026\n\nEast Building\, Level B\, Meymandi E
 xhibition Gallery\n\nKnowing the West embraces and reexamines perceptions 
 of the American West to create more inclusive and complex dialogues. The e
 xhibition reflects the diverse perspectives that have contributed to art a
 nd life in the region. Presenting Native American works together with art 
 by non-Native makers\, it reveals how the stories we tell and the visual l
 anguage we employ influence understanding of our nation’s history and cu
 ltures.
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art
SUMMARY:Knowing the West
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/knowing-the-west
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260731T040428Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52992359000200
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DESCRIPTION:This self-paced course runs from Tuesday\, June 16 to Tuesday\,
  August 11. Participants can start any time between June 16 and August 4.\
 n\nHow can art be used to develop student growth in literacy skills? This 
 self-paced online course explores methods for integrating art and literacy
  strategies to support North Carolina’s Literacy Instruction Standards a
 cross classrooms. Participants gain an understanding of how literacy is de
 fined through a variety of lenses and apply their learning by developing a
  lesson plan. Strategies that incorporate NCMA works of art are used to pr
 actice and apply activities to build interpretive and expressive modes of 
 literacy focused on a variety of reading materials\, comprehension\, vocab
 ulary building\, and writing. This course is designed for teachers of all 
 disciplines and audiences. A certificate of participation for 20 hours wil
 l be provided for literacy\, general\, or content area credits (2 CEU\, wi
 th prior approval from the local school system).
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:NCMA Online Course for Educators: Art and Literacy
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ncma-online-course-for-educa
 tors-art-and-literacy
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260731T040428Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52745325329922
DTSTART:20260802T110000Z
DTEND:20260803T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt at Elk Knob Sta
 te Park. Journey through northern hardwood forest\, follow winding mountai
 n trails\, and explore the unique ecosystems of this high-elevation park. 
 Keep your eyes open—what signs of wildlife or weather-shaped landscapes 
 will you uncover? Look for unique rocks that make Elk Knob a very special 
 clue in North Carolina’s geologic history. Start at the Visitor Center a
 nd scan the QR code in your Actionbound app. Flyers with the QR code will 
 be placed in the Park Office and on all park map kiosks. \n\nThe adventure
 s are available on the Actionbound app – a free download to your cellpho
 ne through your phone’s app store. There’s no need to create a profile
  and no personal data is collected with Actionbound. You simply find new h
 unts by searching for the park name or scanning the associated QR code pos
 ted for your park’s adventure.\n\nThis program is made possible through 
 a partnership with the NC Science Trail (ncsciencetrail.org)! Visit their 
 website for more Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunts being held in oth
 er NC State Parks and for other programs being offered throughout the stat
 e. \n\nThis scavenger hunt is running now through August 31\, 2026.
GEO:36.333462;-81.696432
LOCATION:Elk Knob State Park
SUMMARY:Elk Knob State Park: Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/elk-knob-state-park-curious-
 minds-adventure-scavenger-hunt
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Homeschool & Education Days
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
