DESCRIPTION:Step back in time and discvoer what it took to keep clothes cle
 an in colonial America. Before washing machines\, detergents\, and dryers\
 , laundry was an all-day chore that required hard work\, skill\, and patie
 nce. Learn about tools\, techniques\, and traditions used by early America
 n families\, from making soap to scrubbing\, rinsing\, and drying clothes.
 \n\nAs part of the America250 commemoration\, this historical program expl
 ores the everyday lives of the people who helped build a new nation. By lo
 oking at a ordinary household task\, we'll gain a deeper understanding for
  the resilience\, resourcefulness\, and labor that shaped colonial life. \
 n\nThis program is suitable for all ages. Come ready to learn\, ask questi
 ons\, and experience a glimpse of daily life in early America!\n\nProgram 
 will be held at the beside the visitor center and is weather dependent. Pl
 ease call the visitor center with questions.
