 stuarine habitats surrounding Hammocks Beach State Park. This ranger-led a
 dventure will explore the plants\, animals\, and natural processes that ma
 ke our coastal ecosystems so unique. Keep an eye out for birds\, dolphins\
 , crabs\, and other wildlife as we discuss the importance of estuaries and
  their role in supporting life along the North Carolina coast. Limited to 
 11 participants\; sign-up is required. Contact the park to register at 910
 -326-4881.
