DESCRIPTION:History at High Noon is back! Join us as we relaunch this serie
 s by examining the incredible story of Operation Bumblebee.\n\nSpeaker: Lo
 rraine Makey\, Manager of the Missiles and More Museum on Topsail Island\n
 \nYour favorite virtual lunchtime lecture series is back! Join us as we ki
 ck off the latest installment of History at High Noon by hearing about Ope
 ration Bumblebee. On a barrier island off the coast of North Carolina stan
 d seven concrete towers\, a lonely testament to a top secret project. In t
 he late 1940s\, US Navy secret experiments created a new type of propulsio
 n that revolutionized how we protected our Navy ships. Additionally\, thes
 e barrier-breaking discoveries enabled jets’ flights into the supersonic
  reaches of outer space. This is the incredible story of Operation Bumbleb
 ee.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:History at High Noon: Operation Bumblebee
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-at-high-noon-operati
 on-bumblebee
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
