DESCRIPTION:Join the New Bern Historical Society as they host author Dennis
  Harper as he presents "August Reign of Terror\, Major James H. Craig's Pu
 nitive Raid of August 1781".  He'll be the guest at the updoming Lunch & L
 earn on August 27 at 11:30am at Carolina Colours Pavilion. Reservations at
  www.NewBernHistorical.org or 252-638-8558.\n\nOn January 28\, 1781\, Maj.
  James H. Craig\, with his British forces\, captured the town of Wilmingto
 n. His mission was to establish a supply base for Lt. Gen. Charles Cornwal
 lis’s army as they continued their southern campaign into North Carolina
 . Major Craig’s most notable military expedition was his punitive raid t
 hat began on August 1\, 1781\, when he left Wilmington and headed to Dupli
 n County. From there\, he led his troops toward New Bern\, skirmishing alo
 ng the way with militia. In his program author Dennis Harper will discuss 
 Craig's activities over 10 months of occupation of Wilmington\, NC which i
 ncludes 5 skirmishes in Jones County\, the ransacking of New Bern in Crave
 n County\, the deaths of Capt. John Gordon and Dr. Alexander Gaston and mu
 ch more.
