DESCRIPTION:Join us at Mayo River State Park for our August Full Moon Night
  Hike!\n\nThe full moon of August is called the "Sturgeon Moon" in referen
 ce to the abundance of sturgeon fish in North American lakes in rivers as 
 they are the continents largest fresh water fish. \n\nThis hike will be al
 ong the 2-mile Mayo Mountain Loop\; an easy-moderate hike with plenty of f
 oliage and a steady incline. Please bring water\, hiking shoes\, and flash
 lights.\n\nEvent is subject to cancel due to poor weather. Please click th
 e "I'm Interested" button as event will cancel when there are no registrat
