DESCRIPTION:Celebrate National Public Lands Day with a Tails & Trails Quest
 ! \n\nLooking for a fun way to celebrate National Public Lands Day? Join u
 s for the next Tails & Trails Quest on Saturday\, September 26 at 10:00 am
 !\n\nThis self-guided adventure takes place along the Holly Discovery Trai
 l—a scenic\, family-friendly\, one-mile loop that's perfect for hikers o
 f all ages (and their four-legged friends!).\n\nAlong the trail you'll dis
 cover:\n Interactive educational stations\n A fun quest to complete\n Fasc
 inating facts about the plants\, wildlife\, and natural history of Lake Ja
 mes\n Learn more about the growing Fonta Flora State Trail and how it's co
 nnecting communities across Western North Carolina.\n\nWhether you're expl
 oring with your kids\, walking the dog\, or simply looking for a beautiful
  way to spend the day outdoors\, this event is designed to help you connec
 t with nature while supporting the future of trails in our region.\n\nEven
 t Details\n Saturday\, September 26\n Holly Discovery Trail\, Lake James S
 tate Park\n Approximately 1-mile loop\n Family-friendly\n Dog-friendly\n F
 ree to participate\n\nCome celebrate our public lands\, enjoy one of North
  Carolina's most beautiful state parks\, and discover why every mile of th
 e Fonta Flora State Trail matters.\n\nWe hope to see you on the trail!
GEO:34.683285;-78.594668
LOCATION:Jones Lake State Park
SUMMARY:Tails & Trails Quest
