UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51825974196162
DTSTART:20261121T170000Z
DTEND:20261121T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Learn how early Americans prepared and cooked for large dinner 
 parties like what most of us experience during the Thanksgiving holiday. O
 ur costumed interpreters will demonstrate how to cook a fall harvest meal 
 over an open hearth in the Hoggatt House. Food samples are unavailable to 
 the public. Demonstration only. FREE. All ages welcome. Drop-in.
GEO:35.979741;-79.992174
LOCATION:High Point Museum
SUMMARY:Open Hearth Cooking Demonstration in the Historical Park
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/open-hearth-cooking-demonstr
 ation-in-the-historical-park
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
