DTEND:20270115T173000Z
DESCRIPTION:The NC Public Librarian Certification Commission was formed in 
 1936 to set minimum standards for public librarians to protect and maintai
 n public library resources\, to assure professional management and adminis
 tration of library services\, to meet the personnel requirements for State
  Aid administered by the Library of NC\, and to guarantee the best possibl
 e public library service to all North Carolinians.\n\nThe North Carolina G
 eneral Statute 143B-68 states that the commission must be comprised of: th
 e Chairman of the public libraries section of NCLA\, two individuals named
  by the Governor upon nomination of the NCLA\, the dean of a State or regi
 onally accredited graduate school of librarianship in North Carolina appoi
 nted by the Governor\, and one member at large appointed by the Governor. 
 Commission members appointed by the Governor serve 4-year terms\, all othe
 rs serve 2-year terms.\n\nCommission meetings are held quarterly to review
  applications and discuss Certification policies and procedures.\n\nThe co
 mmission's meeting dates for the 2025-2026 year are October 27\, 2025\, Ja
 nuary 9\, 2026\, April 10\, 2026\, and July 10\, 2026. All meetings are he
 ld at the Library of NC beginning at 1:00 pm unless otherwise posted. Info
 rmation about meetings can be found on the North Carolina Secretary of Sta
 te's meeting calendar.\n\nHave questions about certification? Contact us a
 t NC.Certification.Commission@dncr.nc.gov.
GEO:32.071865;-81.092949
LOCATION:DNCR \, 308
SUMMARY:NC Public Librarian Certification Commission
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/nc-public-librarian-certific
 ation-commission-2701
CATEGORIES:Organizational
CATEGORIES:Public Meetings
END:VEVENT
